# Email delivery — the contact form sends through Resend.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in the values. That file is git-ignored and
# never deployed. On Vercel, add the same keys under Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables instead — do NOT commit a .env.local.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY  From Resend → API Keys → Create API Key.
#                Starts with "re_". Sending-only is enough; the form never
#                needs read or delete access.
#
# CONTACT_FROM    The verified sender. Two options:
#
#                (recommended) "GrowthYari <hello@growthyari.com>"
#                Requires the domain verified in Resend — see the DNS
#                records below. Mail then authenticates via SPF/DKIM and is
#                very unlikely to land in spam.
#
#                (no DNS needed) "GrowthYari <onboarding@resend.dev>"
#                Works immediately, but your recipients see a Resend
#                address in the From field and SPF/DKIM will not match.
#                Fine for testing, not for a live site.
#
# The recipient is hardcoded in data/contact.ts as contactEmail and is NOT
# configurable here, so the inbox the site publishes is always the same one
# the form delivers to. That is deliberate: a mismatch between the two is a
# way to silently lose enquiries.

RESEND_API_KEY=
CONTACT_FROM="GrowthYari <hello@growthyari.com>"